.TH RWWWANCONFIG.INI 5 "2026-11-20" "rolling-linux 2.1.11" "Rolling WWAN Services Manual"
.SH NAME
rwwwanConfig.ini \- runtime configuration file for the rolling_config service
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rwwwanConfig.ini
is the runtime configuration of the
.BR rolling_config (8)
service.  It uses the INI format: a single
.B [Setting]
section with
.I key=value
pairs; lines starting with
.B #
are comments.
.PP
The file is not shipped as a package file.  It is seeded into
.I /etc/rolling/config_file/rolling_config_service/
from the per\-OEM template under
.IB /usr/share/linux\-apps/config_set/ <project>_<oem>/
by
.B seed_config.sh
(called best\-effort by the package post\-install script and again by
the
.B rolling_seed_config.service
first\-boot oneshot while the file is missing).  Seeding never
overwrites an existing file, so local edits survive upgrades;
.B dpkg \-\-purge
removes the file together with
.IR /etc/rolling .
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Start_Service
.B 1
run the configuration service (default),
.B 0
keep the service disabled.
.TP
.B Debug_level
Syslog\-style log level:
.B 7
DEBUG,
.B 6
INFO (default),
.B 5
NOTICE,
.B 4
WARNING,
.B 3
ERROR,
.B 2
CRITICAL.
.TP
.B disable_at_auto_report
.B 1
disable the modem AT auto report,
.B 0
enable it.
.TP
.B set_suspend_radio
.B 1
enable radio suspend,
.B 0
disable it.
.TP
.B Sim_slots_switch
.B 0
do nothing,
.B 1
switch to SIM card slot 1 (default),
.B 2
switch to SIM card slot 2.
.TP
.B Fcc_lock_enable
.B 0
do nothing,
.B 1
disable the FCC lock,
.B 2
enable it.
.TP
.B Wdisable_enable
.B 0
do nothing,
.B 1
disable (default),
.B 2
enable.
.TP
.B Gnss_enable
.B 0
do nothing,
.B 1
disable,
.B 2
enable GNSS.
.TP
.B Band_config_enable
.B 0
do nothing,
.B 1
disable,
.B 2
apply the band configuration.
.TP
.B Net_type_enable
.B 0
do nothing,
.B 1
2G,
.B 2
3G,
.B 3
4G (default),
.B 4
5G.
.TP
.B Disable_esim
.B 0
do nothing,
.B 1
disable the eSIM.
.TP
.B CustomizationSolutionType
.B 1
disable the FbWwanConfig service (default),
.B 2
SarIndex mapped by software and BIOS,
.B 3
SarIndex mapped by SarIndexMappingTable.xml.
.TP
.B SarDownloadType
How the SAR parameter is written to the modem:
.B 1
by image flash (default),
.B 2
by SarConfigValuesTable.xml mapping and AT commands.
.TP
.B ProjectType
.B 0
do nothing (default),
.B 1
L860,
.B 2
L860 R+ HP,
.B 3
L860 R+ Lenovo.
.TP
.B SarType
.B 0
none (default),
.B 1
BodySAR,
.B 2
TA SAR.
.TP
.B SarMapType
.B 0
do nothing (default),
.B 1
to
.B 5
select MapType_1 to MapType_5 from
DeviceModeToScenarioIndexMappingTable.xml.
.TP
.B BodysarState
BodySAR control:
.B 0
do nothing (default),
.B 1
hardware,
.B 2
software.
.TP
.B TASarState
TA SAR control:
.B 0
do nothing (default),
.B 1
hardware,
.B 2
software.
.TP
.B AntTurnerState
Antenna tuner:
.B 0
do nothing (default),
.B 1
disable,
.B 2
enable.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/rolling/config_file/rolling_config_service/rwwwanConfig.ini
Runtime configuration.
.TP
.IB /usr/share/linux\-apps/config_set/ <project>_<oem>/
Per\-OEM templates shipped by the package.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
[Setting]
Start_Service=1
Debug_level=6
disable_at_auto_report=1
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rolling_config (8),
.BR FwUpdate.ini (5)
